---

## 6. RFID Plot Identification

An RC522 RFID reader is used to identify different plots.

Each plot can have its own RFID card or tag.

For example:

```text
RFID → PLOT-A01
RFID → PLOT-A02
RFID → PLOT-B01
```

When the rover detects a tag, the plot ID is sent to the edge device and associated with the next inspection.

This makes it possible to keep records based on location rather than only storing a sequence of images.

---

## 7. Edge AI Device

A smartphone is used as the edge computing device.

The phone receives images from the inspection system and runs the trained plant-health model locally.

The model is trained using a dataset collected from a suitable agricultural dataset source and developed using a cloud development environment such as Google Colab.

The development process is:

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Pre-processing
   ↓
Model Training
   ↓
Testing / Validation
   ↓
Model Optimization
   ↓
Deployable Model
   ↓
Smartphone
```

During normal operation, the phone can perform inference locally instead of sending every image to a cloud server.

This reduces dependence on internet connectivity and makes the system more suitable for areas with limited or unreliable network access.

---

## 8. Communication

The ESP32-S3 and smartphone exchange information during an inspection.

The communication layer carries information such as:

* Plot ID
* Gas sensor readings
* Rover status
* Camera/inspection commands
* AI classification result
* AI confidence
* Inspection status

The exact communication method can be changed depending on the final prototype implementation. The system is designed so that the robot control code and AI application remain separate.

---

## 9. LCD Display

An I2C LCD is connected to the ESP32-S3.

The LCD provides basic information directly on the robot without requiring the user to look at the phone.

Example:

```text
PLOT: B-02
TOMATO

STATUS: ATTENTION
AI: 91%

VOC: 327
```

The LCD is mainly intended for quick status information. More detailed results are shown on the smartphone dashboard.

---

## 10. Smartphone Dashboard

The smartphone provides the main user interface.

The dashboard can display:

* Current plot
* Plant type
* Camera image
* AI result
* Confidence
* Gas sensor reading
* Inspection history
* Rover connection status

Example:

```text
--------------------------------
       PLANT INSPECTION
--------------------------------

Plot: B-02
Plant: Tomato

[ Camera Image ]

Possible Disease
Confidence: 91.4%

VOC Reading: 327
Risk: Moderate

Further inspection recommended

--------------------------------
```

The dashboard is also intended to keep inspection records so that previous observations can be reviewed later.

